# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
env/
.venv/
.env

# Data (large files - regenerate with scripts in src/data, don't commit)
data/raw/*
data/splits/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/splits/.gitkeep

# Cloned baseline repos (each has its own git history/license - don't nest them)
src/data/baselines/*
!src/data/baselines/README.md
!src/data/baselines/__init__.py
notebooks/data/

# Model checkpoints and generated results.
# Everything under results/ is regenerated, never committed. This is broader
# than listing extensions on purpose: the training loop and the ladder both
# write .json into results/, and a DUMMY_PLACEHOLDER file committed by accident
# is a placeholder number sitting in the repo looking like a finding.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
results/*
!results/.gitkeep

# Exception: the small summary tables the paper quotes. A number that appears
# in results.md, STATUS.md or the draft has to be traceable to a versioned
# file, and split_summary.md was the only record of the split counts.
# Checkpoints, per-run JSON and figures stay ignored -- these are tables only.
!results/*.md
!results/*.csv
# ...but never a synthetic run. This rule comes last so it wins: a
# DUMMY_PLACEHOLDER file committed by accident is a placeholder number sitting
# in the repo looking like a finding.
results/*DUMMY_PLACEHOLDER*

# OS/editor junk
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

baselines/**/data/
baselines/**/dataset/
# ...and the plural. DrugBAN's is `datasets/` (140 MB of BindingDB/BioSNAP/Human
# splits); the singular rule above silently did not match it, and 210k lines of
# someone else's benchmark data were staged before this was caught (2026-09-18).
baselines/**/datasets/
baselines/**/image/

# Raw KLIFS API caches (re-fetchable; the per-pair provenance that matters is in
# data/<dataset>_drug_sites_report.json, which records every PDB entry used)
data/klifs_structures.json
data/klifs_ligands.json
